{"timestamp":1774854621751,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"a72715f1-674f-40f3-98c0-46f372cf87c5","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LZjGWLEZUNrJdNkSwV1otM","payload":{"session_id":"a72715f1-674f-40f3-98c0-46f372cf87c5","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-c217d2e7/a72715f1-674f-40f3-98c0-46f372cf87c5.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c217d2e7","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c217d2e7/.pinata/specs/issue-6-adw-c217d2e7-sdlc_planner-geo-tiered-cta-mode-toggle.md","content":"# Plan: Geo-tiered CTA mode toggle \u2014 settings-based buy/trial swap at hydrate level\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd a `ctaMode` settings flag (values: `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only`) delivered per locale via the existing MAS-IO settings pipeline. At hydration time in `web-components`, `hydrate.js` reads this flag and suppresses the non-active CTA type from the DOM \u2014 no card fragment content is modified. Studio gains a settings UI for admins to configure the mode per geo tier (T1\u2013T4) or individual country.\n\n## Task Description\n\n- New `ctaMode` setting definition in `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` (io/www)\n- IO settings transformer delivers `ctaMode` in the per-locale settings payload\n- `hydrate.js` `processCTAs` reads `settings.ctaMode` and:\n  - Hides non-active CTAs (dual-CTA placements: d2p + twp)\n  - Falls back to a Learn More link for single-CTA placements that conflict with the active mode\n  - Fully removes suppressed CTAs from the DOM with `aria-hidden` + `tabindex=-1`\n- Studio Settings UI: new `ctaMode` field with geo/tier selectors (T1\u2013T4 or individual country)\n- P1 features (page exclusion engine, CTA pairing enforcement, preview QA) are deferred to follow-on issues\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Reason |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js` | Edit | Add `ctaMode` to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` and `SETTING_NAME_BY_VALUE` |\n| `web-components/src/hydrate.js` | Edit | Add `applyCTAMode()` helper called inside `processCTAs()` using `settings.ctaMode` |\n| `web-components/src/constants.js` | Edit | Add `CTA_MODE` enum (`default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only`) if not present |\n| `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js` | Edit | Export `ctaMode` definition with editor type `enum` |\n| `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js` | Edit | Add geo-tier UI section for `ctaMode` field |\n| `web-components/test/hydrate.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `applyCTAMode` \u2014 dual-CTA suppression + Learn More fallback |\n| `io/www/test/` | Edit | Add settings transformer test for `ctaMode` extraction and delivery |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `ctaMode` to the IO settings definitions\n\n- In `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`, append to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS`:\n  ```js\n  { name: 'ctaMode', valueType: 'text', editor: 'enum' }\n  ```\n- Confirm `SETTING_NAME_BY_VALUE` map picks it up automatically (it is built from `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS`).\n- Confirm `extractValue` returns the text value for `valuetype: 'text'` (it does \u2014 no extra changes needed to `extractValue`).\n- Run `node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`\n\n### 2. Add `CTA_MODE` constant to web-components\n\n- In `web-components/src/constants.js`, locate the existing `TWP`/`D2P` block (lines 161\u2013162) and add:\n  ```js\n  export const CTA_MODE = {\n      DEFAULT:    'default',\n      BUY_ONLY:   'buy-only',\n      TRIAL_ONLY: 'trial-only',\n  };\n  ```\n- Run `node --check web-components/src/constants.js`\n\n### 3. Implement `applyCTAMode` in hydrate.js\n\n- Add a new exported function `applyCTAMode(footer, ctaMode, learnMoreFallback)`:\n  - Accepts the footer `div[slot]` element, the `ctaMode` string, and an optional `learnMoreFallback` URL.\n  - If `ctaMode` is `default` or falsy, return immediately (no-op).\n  - Identify CTAs with `data-wcs-osi` as checkout links; distinguish d2p vs. twp via `data-plan-type` attribute on the anchor/button (the authoring contract \u2014 see Step 6).\n  - For `buy-only`: suppress all elements whose `data-plan-type === 'twp'`.\n  - For `trial-only`: suppress all elements whose `data-plan-type === 'd2p'`.\n  - Suppression = `el.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true'); el.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1'); el.style.display = 'none';` then remove from DOM.\n  - If after suppression no visible CTAs remain (single-CTA placement that conflicts):\n    - If `learnMoreFallback` is provided, inject `<a href=\"${learnMoreFallback}\" class=\"learn-more-fallback spectrum-Button spectrum-Button--secondary spectrum-Button--sizeM\"><span class=\"spectrum-Button-label\">Learn More</span></a>`.\n    - Otherwise log a warning: `console.warn('ctaMode: no CTA remains and no learnMoreFallback configured')`.\n- Import `CTA_MODE` from `./constants.js`.\n- In `processCTAs`, after `footer.append(...ctas)` and `merchCard.append(footer)`, call:\n  ```js\n  const { ctaMode, learnMoreUrl } = fields;\n  if (ctaMode) applyCTAMode(footer, ctaMode, learnMoreUrl);\n  ```\n- Run `node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js`\n\n### 4. Update Studio setting-name-map.js\n\n- In `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js`, the map already delegates to `SETTING_NAME_BY_VALUE` from the IO transformer, so `ctaMode` becomes available automatically after Step 1.\n- No code change needed; verify the import chain is intact.\n\n### 5. Add ctaMode field to Studio Settings UI\n\n- In `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js`, add a new settings section for **CTA Mode** alongside existing settings fields:\n  - Label: `CTA Mode`\n  - A `<sp-picker>` (or equivalent) with options: `Default`, `Buy Only`, `Trial Only` \u2014 stored as `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only`.\n  - A geo/tier selector: checkboxes or a multi-select for T1 (`us,gb,fr,de,jp,au,nz`), T2, T3, T4, or specific country locales \u2014 stored as locale overrides on the settings fragment.\n  - The UI writes the setting using the existing `settings-store.js` pattern (create/update a settings entry fragment with `name: 'ctaMode'`, `valuetype: 'text'`, `textValue: <selected mode>`, and `locales: [<selected locales>]`).\n- Run `node --check studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js`\n\n### 6. Define authoring contract for `data-plan-type` on CTA links\n\n- Document (in a code comment in `hydrate.js`) that authors must set `data-plan-type=\"d2p\"` or `data-plan-type=\"twp\"` on CTA anchor elements in AEM content for the swap to identify CTA type.\n- Add `learnMoreUrl` to the recognized fields list in hydrate (no new processing needed beyond reading `fields.learnMoreUrl`).\n\n### 7. Write unit tests \u2014 web-components\n\n- In `web-components/test/hydrate.test.js`, add tests for `applyCTAMode`:\n  - `ctaMode=default` \u2192 no CTAs removed.\n  - `ctaMode=buy-only`, dual CTAs (d2p + twp) \u2192 twp CTA removed, d2p remains.\n  - `ctaMode=trial-only`, dual CTAs \u2192 d2p removed, twp remains.\n  - `ctaMode=buy-only`, single twp CTA, with `learnMoreUrl` \u2192 CTA removed, Learn More link injected.\n  - `ctaMode=buy-only`, single twp CTA, no `learnMoreUrl` \u2192 CTA removed, warning logged.\n\n### 8. Write unit tests \u2014 IO settings transformer\n\n- In the IO test suite, add a test confirming `ctaMode` is returned in the settings object when the settings fragment contains a `ctaMode` entry with `valuetype: 'text'`.\n- Run `node --check` on any new test files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- `ctaMode` appears in `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` and is delivered in the settings payload for any locale.\n- `hydrate.js` exports `applyCTAMode`; it is called after CTAs are appended to the DOM.\n- When `ctaMode=buy-only`, all TWP CTAs are absent from the DOM after hydration.\n- When `ctaMode=trial-only`, all D2P CTAs are absent from the DOM after hydration.\n- When the conflicting CTA is the only CTA and `learnMoreUrl` is set, a Learn More link replaces it.\n- Studio Settings UI renders a `ctaMode` picker and geo/tier locale selector; saving writes a settings entry fragment.\n- No card content fragments are modified at any point.\n- All new JS files pass `node --check`.\n\n## Validation Commands\n\n- `node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js`\n- `node --check web-components/src/constants.js`\n- `node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js`\n- `cd web-components && npm test -- --grep \"applyCTAMode\"` (after tests are added)\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LZjGWLEZUNrJdNkSwV1otM"}}
